    "bands": [
      {
        "id": "identity-band",
        "kind": "identity",
        "step": "authority",
        "text": "Identity: users act with their own Entra identity, and Fabric permissions decide what each one sees (on-behalf-of). The writer is a separate, least-privilege identity."
      },
      {
        "id": "policy-band",
        "kind": "policy",
        "step": "authority",
        "text": "Authority: models propose, deterministic policy validates, a human approves, and only the scoped writer writes. MCP access and gateway policy never replace backend authorization."
      },
      {
        "id": "evidence-band",
        "kind": "evidence",
        "step": "evidence",
        "text": "Evidence: every hop carries a correlation ID and an execution label. A configured server, a tool description or an existing item is not proof that an operation ran."
      }
    ],
    "columns": 7,
    "cue": "Build it one layer at a time. Fabric first, because the answer is only as good as the governed data and definitions. Then Foundry for reasoning. Then MCP for access. Then authority, because access is not permission. Then evidence, because a claim without proof is not a result.",
